
### 1. Patient Service
GET http://localhost:8082/health

### 2. Availability Service
GET http://localhost:8083/health

### 3. Notification Service
GET http://localhost:8084/health

### 4. Appointment Service
GET http://localhost:8081/health


### Create a patient
POST http://localhost:8082/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test 3 Patient",
  "email": "e2e3.patient@example.com"
}

### get eligibility
GET http://localhost:8082/api/patients/4/eligibility


### Create a doctor
POST http://localhost:8083/api/v1/doctors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dr. E2E Test 2",
  "specialty": "General Medicine"
}


### Create an appointment slot
POST http://localhost:8083/api/v1/slots
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "doctorId": 3,
  "startsAt": "2027-01-15T09:00:00Z",
  "endsAt": "2027-01-15T09:30:00Z",
  "capacity": 5
}


### Book an appointment
POST http://localhost:8081/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: e2e-booking-003

{
  "patientId": 4,
  "slotId": 3
}

### Replay the same booking — same key and same body
POST http://localhost:8081/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-booking-replay-001

{
  "patientId": 1,
  "slotId": 2
}

### Reuse the same key with a different body — expect a conflict
POST http://localhost:8081/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-booking-replay-001

{
  "patientId": 2,
  "slotId": 2
}

